+### Score 10x
+
+While Score 10x is On, score gains through the score-add function are multiplied by 10. The function (Asia `0x47a560`; the US 1.00 store is `0x47B229`) takes the gain in `esi` and adds it to two fields of the score object, `+0x1c` and the total `+0x80`, each clamped to 99,999,999 and floored at 0; the hook sits at the function's entry and multiplies a positive gain, capped so the product never passes the maximum, so the function's own clamp still holds. Losses are not multiplied. The US 1.00 table has no score hook yet (the entry on that image is unverified), so the cheat installs nothing there. The sibling score helper (Asia `0x47a5b0`, fields `+0x20`/`+0x84`) is not hooked, so gains through it are not multiplied; whether every score gain flows through the hooked function was not proved statically and is what the real game test should watch.
